WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 6: My Five Senses.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.720
In this unit you will learn about your five senses.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.240
They are seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting and touching.

4
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.620
You will learn the part of your body you use for each one.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.480
You will learn describing words
like soft, loud, sweet and cold.

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.840
You will begin to compare things.

7
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.160
A tree is tall.

8
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.480
A building is taller.

9
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.120
Most of all you will explore the world around you.

10
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.840
Stay curious, and be thankful for all
the wonderful things you can sense.

11
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.980
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

12
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:46.320
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
the five senses: see, hear, smell, taste, touch.

13
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:52.500
You will also point to and name the body
parts we use: eyes, ears, nose, tongue, hands.

14
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.160
You will also say which sense goes with
which body part (“I see with my eyes”).

15
00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.940
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:07.340
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: ship, shop, dish, shell, brush, chip.

17
00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.620
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

18
00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.820
The reading sequence includes Amal at
the Market and Talk about My Five Senses.

19
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.340
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

20
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.120
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

21
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.720
The first language focus is Eyes are for seeing.

22
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.500
Point to your eyes and say the whole sentence.

23
00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.680
Your eyes are the sense that helps you see.

24
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.440
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

25
00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.740
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

26
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.340
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

27
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:57.560
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

28
00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.400
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:05.500
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

30
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.960
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
